<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>For each circle on the earth's surface, choose whether it is a great circle, a small circle or half of a great circle.</p><p>(a) a circle on the earth's surface whose radius is <m>3000\,\text{km}</m>: [ a great circle | a small circle | half of a great circle ]  </p><p>(b) the equator: [ a great circle | a small circle | half of a great circle ]  </p><p>(c) the parallel of latitude <m>1^\circ\,17'\,\mathrm{S}</m>, through Nairobi: [ a great circle | a small circle | half of a great circle ]  </p><p>(d) the meridian <m>37^\circ\,\mathrm{E}</m>, from the North Pole to the South Pole: [ a great circle | a small circle | half of a great circle ]  </p><p>(e) the circle cut by a plane through the centre of the earth, Mombasa and Lodwar: [ a great circle | a small circle | half of a great circle ]  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>A great circle is a circle on the sphere whose plane passes through the centre, so its radius is the radius of the sphere. Any other circle on the sphere is a small circle. A meridian runs from pole to pole on one side of the earth, so it is half of a great circle.</p><ul><li>(a) a circle on the earth's surface whose radius is <m>3000\,\text{km}</m>: a small circle. Its radius is less than <m>6370\,\text{km}</m>, so its plane does not pass through the centre: a small circle.</li><li>(b) the equator: a great circle. The plane of the equator passes through the centre of the earth, so the equator is a great circle.</li><li>(c) the parallel of latitude <m>1^\circ\,17'\,\mathrm{S}</m>, through Nairobi: a small circle. This parallel is close to the equator, but its plane does not pass through the centre, so its radius <m>6370\cos 1^\circ\,17'\,\text{km}</m> is less than <m>6370\,\text{km}</m>: a small circle.</li><li>(d) the meridian <m>37^\circ\,\mathrm{E}</m>, from the North Pole to the South Pole: half of a great circle. A meridian runs from pole to pole on one side only. It is half of a great circle; the other half is the meridian <m>143^\circ\,\mathrm{W}</m>.</li><li>(e) the circle cut by a plane through the centre of the earth, Mombasa and Lodwar: a great circle. Any plane through the centre cuts the sphere in a great circle.</li></ul></p></solution>
    <answer><p>a small circle</p></answer>
    <answer><p>a great circle</p></answer>
    <answer><p>a small circle</p></answer>
    <answer><p>half of a great circle</p></answer>
    <answer><p>a great circle</p></answer>
</stack-static>